you don't get it really. Subclass already have functions because it was extending `MessageInterface` and `MailerInterface`. the only different the MailPanel is hardcoded to `getSwiftMessage()`, it should be `getMessage()`,  dont make it complicated @Ragazzo , it's just renaming method simple as that.

imagine I have Subclass called `SendGrid` or `MailGun`... they don't use `SwiftMessage()`

in order to make it work properly. code would be like this, I don't think this is right, the name is `getSwiftMessage` but in reality I'm returning `send grid class`

``` php
public function getSwiftMessage() {
        if (!is_object($this->_sendGridMessage)) {
            $this->_sendGridMessage = new \SendGrid\Email();
        }
        return $this->_sendGridMessage;
}
```

remember that MessageInterface is on Core.. while the ext-debug is only an extensions. core and extensions don't work properly?
